# Plugins & themes — bulk flow (mandatory)

When changing SiteDetail actions, library installs, **wp-proxy**, or **wphubpro-bridge** plugin/theme handlers, follow this contract. Full reference: **`.cursor/docs/FUNCTIONS.md`** (wp-proxy section) · **`functions/wp-proxy/README.md`** · **`wphubpro-bridge/README.md`**.

---

## End-to-end path

```
Hub UI → extensionBulkFromSite / library*Install
      → postBridgeApiJsonWithMeta({ siteId, handler, body })
      → wp-proxy (resolve ZIPs, normalize)
      → wphubpro-bridge REST (bulk POST)
      → WordPress
```

---

## Request contract (Hub → wp-proxy → bridge)

1. **Always** send `body.plugins[]` or `body.themes[]` — non-empty **object arrays**. Single-row actions = array length **1**.
2. **Never** send top-level `body.plugin`, `body.slug`, or string-only array entries.
3. **Handler keys** (canonical only): `plugins/install|update|activate|deactivate|uninstall`, `themes/install|update|activate|deactivate|delete`, `bridge/forceUpdate`, `sync`. No aliases (`plugins/de-install`, `themes/uninstall`, underscore forms).
4. **ZIPs:** HTTPS `zip_url` only — wp-proxy resolves library items; **`zip_base64` forbidden**.

---

## Response contract (bridge → wp-proxy → Hub)

All manage endpoints return:

```json
{ "results": [{ "id", "ok", "installed?", "activated?", "error?" }], "succeeded", "failed" }
```

Hub parses with **`summarizeBulkPayload`** in `extensionBulkFromSite.ts` (`BulkItemResult` includes `installed`, `activated`).

---

## wp-proxy forwarding

| Handler | Bridge calls |
|---------|----------------|
| install, activate, deactivate, uninstall, delete | **One** bulk POST |
| plugins/update | Resolve all rows → **≤2** calls: `manage/update` batch + `manage/install` batch (WP.org slug+version) |
| themes/update | **One** bulk `manage/update` POST |

Do **not** loop per-item bridge calls from wp-proxy.

---

## Bridge behavior (do not regress)

| Case | Rule |
|------|------|
| Plugin install | Always activate after install |
| Plugin update | Reactivate if was active |
| Theme bulk install | Install all; activate **only last successful** in array |
| Theme update | Active theme stays active |
| Theme delete | Block delete of active theme |

---

## Platform domain entry points

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `extensionBulkFromSite.ts` | **Unified** bulk + single-item wrappers (`runPluginsBulkForSite`, `runThemesBulkForSite`, …) |
| `pluginUpdateFromSite.ts` / `themeUpdateFromSite.ts` | Update source resolution; still send `[item]` arrays |
| `libraryCollectionInstall.ts` | Per site: `plugins/install` batch + `themes/install` batch (separate calls) |
| `libraryFamilyInstall.ts` | Same batch pattern as collections (not sequential per member) |

Deprecated re-export shims: `pluginActivateFromSite.ts`, `extensionRemoveFromSite.ts`, `themeActivateFromSite.ts` → import from `extensionBulkFromSite.ts` instead.

---

## Docs sync

After changing this flow, update in the **same change set**:

- `.cursor/docs/FUNCTIONS.md` (wp-proxy section)
- `functions/wp-proxy/README.md`
- `wphubpro-bridge/README.md`
- This rule if the contract changes

See **`wphub-docs-sync.mdc`**.

---

## Bridge plugin version (same commit)

Any change under **`wphubpro-bridge/`** that affects runtime behavior must include a **`Version: x.y.z`** bump in **`wphubpro-bridge/wphubpro-bridge.php`** if not already raised in the commit. See **`wphub-bridge-plugin.mdc`**.
